# Veltify Project Rules

## Component Structure
- All components should extend the Base component for consistency
- Use Svelte 5's `$props()` and `$derived` for props and computed values
- Use `$bindable()` for two-way binding when needed
- Use `{@render children()}` for rendering slots
- Keep components focused on a single responsibility
- Compound components should be organized in their own directories

## Styling Patterns
- Each component should have its own CSS file in src/lib/styles/shadcn/
- Use the cls() helper function for generating class names
- Follow the naming convention: [component]-[property]-[value]
- Use theme variables for colors and spacing
- Avoid hardcoded color values; use theme colors instead
- Use Tailwind's @apply directive for composing utility classes

## Theming System
- Theme variables are defined in Base.css using the @theme directive
- Dark mode variants are defined in the .dark selector
- Color variables follow the pattern: --color-[purpose]-[variant]
- Spacing variables follow the pattern: --spacing-[size]
- Use CSS variables for all themeable properties

## File Organization
- Component files go in src/lib/components/
- Complex components get their own directory with related components
- CSS files go in src/lib/styles/shadcn/
- Helper functions go in src/lib/helpers.ts
- All components are exported from src/lib/index.ts

## Naming Conventions
- Component files use PascalCase (e.g., Button.svelte)
- CSS files match component names (e.g., Button.css)
- CSS classes use kebab-case (e.g., button-variant-primary)
- Helper functions use camelCase (e.g., cls())

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Keep components small and focused
- Extract complex logic to helper functions
- Use consistent indentation (2 spaces)

## Accessibility
- All interactive components must be keyboard accessible
- Use appropriate ARIA attributes
- Ensure sufficient color contrast
- Support focus management for complex components
- Test with screen readers

## Development Workflow
- Update the memory bank when making significant changes
- Document new components and features
- Keep the activeContext.md file updated with current work
- Update progress.md when completing milestones
- Test components in isolation before integration

## Release Process
- Update version in package.json
- Update CHANGELOG.md with changes
- Run build and tests before release
- Tag releases in git
- Publish to npm
